{
  "_comment": "tracks: RAW, SmackDown, NXT and big events each have their own last-watched; every episode needs a \"track\": \"raw\", \"smackdown\", \"nxt\" or \"events\". NXT weekly shows and NXT's own big events (TLC, Worlds Collide) go in the nxt track. accounts: the show's official X handles without the @; anything they post is covered as about the show. Edit this file in the spoiler-blocker-data repo on GitHub (pencil icon), not here; npm run pull-data copies it back before a store release. aliases: show names, hashtags and premium live event names that never change. people: wrestlers, managers and factions who have been around a while. weak: keywords that are also everyday words; they only count with a context word, a second keyword, or on an air night. context: wrestling words that back up a weak keyword. seasons: one per calendar year; that year's debuts, new ring names, new factions and storyline words go in its people and terms. episodes: every RAW, SmackDown and premium live event, oldest first, newest last, with the seasonId of its year; premium live events get \"kind\": \"event\". A show that does not start in the evening US Eastern gets \"airTime\": \"HH:MM\" (Eastern), like the Perth event. Keep ids unique. RAW and SmackDown dates after the week of Nov 13, 2026 are the normal Monday/Friday schedule and have not been checked one by one. NXT (added Nov 15 2026): Tuesdays 8 PM ET on The CW. Nov 4 moved to Wednesday (election). Worlds Collide: Doomsday (Dec 15) may replace that week's NXT; start reported as 7:30 or 8 PM, so 19:30 is used (earlier is safer). Jan 5 is expected to be New Year's Evil (not yet announced). Perth: SmackDown Dec 11 and RAW Dec 14 air in the US morning (airTime 04:00 until start times are final); the John Cena Classic (Orlando) is that evening, Dec 14. TO DO: NXT New Year's Evil and Vengeance Day 2027 dates. Never delete or rename an episode id (users have ticked it); to remove one on purpose, also add its id to a \"removedEpisodes\" list, or the extension refuses the file. everyday: weak keywords so ordinary they need backup even on a show night (a wrestling word, a second name, or an author who has been posting about the show); distinctive names like Cody or Rhea stay out of it so they still count alone on show nights.",
